{"id":"st429-3","designation":"ST 429-3","title":"D-Cinema Packaging — Sound and Picture Track File","state":"active","suite":"429","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st429-3/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st429-3/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This standard specifies the common features of the format of sound and picture Tracks Files for distribution of D-Cinema content using the MXF file format. It defines data structures for interchange at the signal interfaces of networks or storage media, but does not define internal storage formats for compliant devices or mappings for particular essence encodings. This document is an Application Specification for D-Cinema applications. It is based on the SMPTE ST 390, but is further constrained to address the needs of distribution of D-Cinema content to exhibition sites.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"D-Cinema Packaging — Sound and Picture Track File","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"Table of contents","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"Foreword","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"1Scope","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"2Conformance","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"3Normative references","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"4Terms and definitions","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"5Overview","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"6Pattern Constraints","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"6.1General","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"6.2Baseline Operational Pattern","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"6.3Additional Constraints","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"7Labeling","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"8Essence Constraints","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.1General","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.2Picture","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"8.3Sound","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"9Header Metadata Constraints","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"9.1General","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"9.2Time Code","page":1},{"level":3,"title":"9.3Track File Identity","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"10Descriptive Metadata Constraints","page":1},{"level":2,"title":"11Other Co